function smart_sort_array($set, $order) {
    usort($set, function($a, $b) use ($order) {
        return $order === 'ASC' ? $a['age'] - $b['age'] : $b['age'] - $a['age'];
    });
    return $set;
}
```

This function uses the `usort()` function to perform the sorting. It creates an anonymous function that takes two elements `$a` and `$b`, and returns their difference in age based on the `$order` parameter passed to the `smart_sort_array()` function. If `$order` is set to `ASC`, we subtract `$b['age']` from `$a['age]` to get a negative value if `$a['age]` is smaller than `$b['age]`. If `$order` is set to `DESC`, we swap the order of subtraction to get a positive value if `$a['age]` is smaller than `$b['age]`. This will sort the elements of the `$set` array based on the age values using the provided `$order` parameter.

