Here's a JavaScript function that takes a string variable in dot notation and returns all entries in an object where the nested key-value pair matches the given string key:

```javascript
function findObjectEntriesByKey(object, key) {
  const entries = [];

  function traverseObject(obj) {
    Object.keys(obj).forEach((k) => {
      if (typeof obj[k] === 'object') {
        traverseObject(obj[k]);
      } else if (key === k || key === `${k}.`) {
        entries.push([k, obj[k]]);
      }
    });
  }

  traverseObject(object);
  return entries;
}
```

To use this function, pass an object as the first argument and the key you want to search for as the second argument. It will return an array of arrays containing the key and value pairs that match the search criteria. If you want to search for a partial key, include a `.` in the second argument to indicate a sub-property. For example:

